    "preamble": "Sachin vs Rakesh Kumar Ahirwar on 1 February, 2018",
    "facts": "ad The brief facts giving rise to this petition are that against the applicant Food Inspector Mandla filed a complaint on 15/04/2009 that M the sample of wheat taken on 02/08/2005 was found to be adulterated of as per the report of Public Analyst dated 16/09/2005 after getting sanction order dated 28/02/2009 on the basis of application dated rt 24/12/2008 under section 7(1)/16(1)(a) of Prevention of Food ou Adulteration Act, 1954 before the CJM, Sagar and the CJM took C cognizance of the offence and proceeding of the criminal case is h pending in which on behalf of the applicant, the application under ig section 468 of Cr.PC was filed on the ground that for the aforesaid H offence maximum punishment is 3 years and under section 368 of Cr.P.C for such cases 3 years limitation for taking cognizance is prescribed and in this case complaint has been filed after expiry of 3 years and there is nothing on record to consider any time for exclusion under section 470 of Cr.P.C but the application was rejected by the learned JMFC stating that from the date of sanction complaint has been filed within time. Against which the revision was preferred, which was also rejected by the Revisional Court by order dated 20/09/2010, hence this petition is filed.",
